<title>USA: DOT report of U.S. airline performance in December.</title>
<headline>DOT report of U.S. airline performance in December.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Transportation</p>
<p>Department Air Travel Consumer Report on the performance of</p>
<p>the 10 largest U.S. air carriers in domestic non-stop flights.</p>
<p>PERCENT OF ON-TIME ARRIVALS:</p>
<p> -	   Dec96  Nov96   1996</p>
<p> Alaska     54.8   68.9   68.6</p>
<p> Amer.West  65.1   74.4   70.8</p>
<p> American   70.0   79.7   72.2</p>
<p> Cont.'l    73.1   80.9   76.6</p>
<p> Delta	66.9   75.0   71.2</p>
<p> Northwest  61.6   75.4   76.6</p>
<p>PERCENT OF ON-TIME ARRIVALS:</p>
<p> -	   Dec96  Nov96   1996</p>
<p> Southwest  67.6   79.2   81.8</p>
<p> TWA	  63.0   76.6   68.5</p>
<p> United     62.4   79.2   73.8</p>
<p> USAir	70.4   80.6   75.7</p>
<p> Total	66.6   77.9   74.5</p>
<p>COMPLAINTS:</p>
<p>    Total Complaints Per	    Mishandled Bags Per</p>
<p>    100,000 Passengers		1,000 Passengers</p>
<p>    -	Dec96  Nov96   1996    Dec96  Nov96   1996</p>
<p> TWA	  0.98   1.20   1.25     8.31   5.20   6.12</p>
<p> United     0.69   0.79   0.74    10.50   6.69   6.73</p>
<p> USAir	0.33   0.33   0.68     6.69   4.72   5.14</p>
<p> Total	0.56   0.68   0.74     7.15   4.87   5.30</p>
<p>The percent of on-time arrivals is based on reports from the 27 airports required to report by the DOT plus voluntary reports from other airports.  </p>
<p>The consumer complaints portion of the report is based on complaints made to the DOT in writing, by telephone or in person. The DOT said it has not determined the validity of the complaints.</p>
<p>Total passenger complaints include flight delays, mishandled bags and oversales. They do not concern charges of safety violations, which are handled by the Federal Aviation Administration.</p>
